				\begin{document}$$E\left[{B}_{x,t}\right]=\left({n}_{s,x,t}+{n}_{m,x,t}\right){f}_{x}$$\end{document}EBx,t=ns,x,t+nm,x,tfxwhere fx is the age-specific average female fecundity rate and ns,x,t and nm,x,t refers to the number of susceptible and immune females, respectively, of age x at time t. The sex of each newborn was then determined by means of a Bernoulli draw with probability given by the proportion of males in the population. Thus, if the draw produced 1 for that individual, it became a male, and if 0 a female.
